      <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Edudel Class 9 Result 2026">
      <div class="blog-body">
        <h1 class="blog-title text-center mb-4">Delhi DoE Class 9 Results 2026 DECLARED: Your Guide to Checking Scores on Edudel.nic.in!</h1>
        <p class="lead">The much-awaited results for the Class 9 annual examinations for the academic session 2025-26 have been officially declared by the Directorate of Education (DoE), Delhi. Students across government and aided schools can now access their scorecards online, marking a significant milestone in their academic journey.</p>

        <div class="highlight-text">
          <p><strong>Breaking News:</strong> The Delhi DoE Class 9 results were announced on March 30, 2026! Access your results directly on the official portal, edudel.nic.in.</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="section-title">How to Check Your Class 9 Result on Edudel.nic.in</h2>
        <p>Checking your Class 9 result is a straightforward process designed for ease of access. Students and parents are advised to keep essential login credentials ready to avoid any delays. Follow these simple steps to view and download your provisional marksheet:</p>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official Website</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">Navigate to the Directorate of Education, Delhi's official website: <a href="https://edudel.nic.in" target="_blank">edudel.nic.in</a>.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">2. Locate the Results Section</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, look for the "What's New" or "Results 2025-26" section. Click on the link specifically for Class 9 results.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">3. Enter Your Login Credentials</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">You will be redirected to a login page where you need to input the required details:
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Student ID</strong> (11-digit)</li>
              <li><strong>Class</strong> (Select 9th)</li>
              <li><strong>Section</strong></li>
              <li><strong>Date of Birth</strong> (in DD/MM/YYYY format)</li>
            </ul>
            Ensure all details are entered accurately to proceed.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">4. View and Download Your Result</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">After entering the details, click on the "Submit" or "View Result" button. Your Class 9 result will be displayed on the screen. It is highly recommended to download the provisional scorecard and save a copy for future reference. You can also take a printout.</div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="section-title">Important Details on Your Scorecard</h2>
        <p>The online marksheet provides a comprehensive overview of your performance. Ensure you carefully check all the details mentioned:</p>

        <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
          <p>✅ Student's Name</p>
          <p>✅ Class and Section</p>
          <p>✅ Date of Birth</p>
          <p>✅ Subject-wise Marks/Grades</p>
          <p>✅ Overall Result Status (Pass/Promoted/Compartment/Fail)</p>
        </div>
        <p>In case of any discrepancies or errors in the details, students should immediately contact their respective school authorities for correction.</p>

        <h2 class="section-title">Understanding the "15-Mark Grace Policy" and Supplementary Exams</h2>
        <p>The Directorate of Education, Delhi, has a supportive policy in place for students who may not have cleared all subjects. It's important to be aware of the "15-mark grace policy."</p>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">Grace Marks Policy</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">This policy allows failing students a total of 15 marks across subjects to reach the 33% passing criteria and gain "Promoted" status. This provides a crucial second chance for students to advance to the next academic level.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">Supplementary/Improvement Exams</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">For those who are unable to pass even with the grace marks, or wish to improve their scores, there will be an opportunity to appear for supplementary or improvement exams. The detailed schedule for these examinations will be shared soon by the respective schools. Successfully clearing these exams will allow students to be promoted to Class 10.</div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="section-title">What's Next?</h2>
        <p>For students who have successfully cleared their Class 9 examinations, congratulations! You will be promoted to Class 10, embarking on an important year leading up to your board exams.</p>
        <p>The digital marksheet serves as provisional proof until schools issue original documents. Schools will also provide physical report cards and detailed performance assessments.</p>
        <p>Stay connected with your school and the official edudel.nic.in website for any further announcements regarding the upcoming academic session and examination schedules.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

            
            
